    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0527" n="1037" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1037"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115/5–2448</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of United
                        Nations Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Rusk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Brigadier General
                            Marshall S. Carter
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-05-24">May 24, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The memorandum of today’s date from Mr. Henderson to the Secretary,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d311-f1"/> with regard to the security of American citizens in the
                    Levant, concludes with the following paragraph: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In connection with the above, it is extremely important that no moves be
                            taken which may further inflame the situation, such as a decision which
                            would lead to the sending of arms to the State of Israel by the United
                            States; action extending <hi rendition="#italic">de jure</hi>
                            recognition of the State of Israel; or further denunciation of the Arabs
                            by American representatives before the Security Council, until our
                            missions in the Near East have been warned and have had an opportunity
                            to take steps to warn American citizens.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>This memorandum has received the approval of the President.</p>
                <p>It is suggested that the Secretary at luncheon tomorrow with Ambassador Austin
                    may wish to draw the substance of this paragraph to the Ambassador’s
                    attention.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
